---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

/**
 * About Badger. First person, first name only, no photo (Ron, 2026-09-08).
 * The Play and App Store listings already carry the full legal name; the site
 * deliberately does not repeat it.
 *
 * This page is the site's only contact surface. Before this page, the three
 * addresses only appeared inside Privacy, Terms and the Programs page, so a
 * reader with a question had nowhere obvious to go. The footer carries both an
 * "About" and a "Contact" link, the second pointing at #contact here.
 *
 * Prose, not headed sections: there is not enough here to earn subheads, and
 * a section per sentence is what made the first draft read as generated. The
 * one remaining h2 is "Get in touch", which stays because #contact is a footer
 * link target.
 *
 * The copy is RON'S OWN WORDS (2026-09-08), edited only for grammar. Do not
 * "improve" the voice: the rhetorical questions, the exclamation marks and the
 * repetition are the point, and every earlier draft written in a smoother
 * register was rejected for sounding machine-written.
 *
 * The free/no-subscription pitch was REMOVED on purpose (Ron, 2026-09-08): it is
 * true, but it is not what this page is for, and the same easing-off applies to
 * the privacy stance over time. /promise still makes the argument in full for
 * anyone who wants it. Do not reintroduce either claim here as a selling point.
 */

const description =
  "Badger is made by one person, not a company. Who builds it, why it exists, and how to get in touch.";

---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={description}>
  <Header currentPath={Astro.url.pathname} />

  <main class="doc">
    <span class="kicker">Who is behind this</span>
    <h1>About Badger</h1>
    <div class="intro">
      <p>
        Hey there, Ron here.
      </p>
      <p>
        Badger was born after years of using an app I really liked, but always felt some
        things were missing. The goal was to build something that supports a wide range of
        use cases, on top of just logging your workout. We all know that using different
        machines for the same exercise doesn't translate to the same working weight. What if
        you travel a lot and go to multiple gyms? Or even just have a gym close to home and
        one close to work? Need to remember which attachment you used? All of those and more
        led me to build Badger.
      </p>
      <p>
        Yes, I built it for myself. Then I figured, it's already built, so why not share it
        with others? Some may find use for it. If it helps and encourages people to stay
        fit, that's a win for me. It's humbling knowing people out there use it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Why Badger? You may be familiar with the viral video of "Honey Badger Don't Care".
        Badgers are fierce, and if you're lifting weights, you're fierce too! No matter if
        you're just starting or if you're an experienced lifter, you are awesome for doing
        it!
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="entry contact" id="contact">
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        I'm here to listen to your feedback, suggestions and ideas. You have the contact
        information, so don't hold back from using it.
      </p>

      <dl class="addresses">
        <div class="address">
          <dt>Anything at all</dt>
          <dd><a href="mailto:hello@badger.fit">hello@badger.fit</a></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="address">
          <dt>Bugs and feature requests</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="mailto:feedback@badger.fit">feedback@badger.fit</a>
            <span class="note">
              Or use <em>Send feedback</em> in the app, which fills in your device and
              version so you don't have to.
            </span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="address">
          <dt>Your data and privacy</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="mailto:privacy@badger.fit">privacy@badger.fit</a>
            <span class="note">
              The <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a> has the full answer.
            </span>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-min">
      <a class="btn-accent" href="/#download">Get the app</a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 60px 24px 0;
  }

  .kicker {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .doc h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 38px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .intro {
    margin-top: 26px;
  }

  .intro p a,
  .note a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-ink) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .intro p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* The one ledger section left: 2px ink top, matching /promise. */
  .entry {
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .entry h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .entry p {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .addresses {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
  }

  .address {
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }

  .address:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }

  .address dt {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .address dd {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .note {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 5px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .cta-min {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .doc {
      padding: 44px 20px 0;
    }

    .doc h1 {
      font-size: 30px;
    }
  }
</style>
